  "prompt_mode": "short_sentence_continuation",
  "prompt_text": "Continue the text below with exactly one short, natural, coherent English sentence. Return only the continuation, with no preamble or explanation:\nA woman has been dating guy after guy, but it never seems to work out. She’s unaware that she’s actually been dating the same guy over and over; a shapeshifter who’s fallen for her, and is certain he’s going to get it right this time.\n\nOne day, the woman and the shapeshifter have date at swanky wine bistro in the trendy part of town. For this \"first date\" the shapeshifter has come as Dirk Haynes, a wealthy man about town.\n\nThe woman is late, and when she arrives, she’s in a hurry. She seems to barely pay attention to any of Dirk's well-chosen lines. She’s distracted, and she’s late for something.\n\nFinally Dirk can't help but ask: \"Am I keeping you from something?\"\n\n\"No, but I’m late for something,\" she says.\n\n\"What are you late for?\" asks Dirk.\n\n\"I’m late for my date with you,\" she says.\n\nThis flummoxed Dirk. \"But you are not late, you're here,\" he said.\n\n\"Yes, but I'm late for my date with you,\" she said.\n\nDirk had an idea. \"Just who do you think I am?\" he asked her.",
  "reference_single_token_nfa_states": 25,
